What Are Home Pregnancy Tests?
Home pregnancy tests are diagnostic devices designed to detect the presence of human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG) hormone in urine samples. Available as sticks, strips, or digital devices, these tests offer women a private, convenient method for early pregnancy confirmation with accuracy levels matching clinical tests when used correctly. The market has evolved from simple line-based tests to sophisticated digital versions featuring smartphone connectivity and weeks estimators, reflecting ongoing innovation in reproductive health diagnostics.
